            "text": "{\"strengths\":[\"The explanation gives a complete causal chain: drought reduces harvests, supply shifts left while demand is unchanged, a shortage occurs at P1, and price rises to P2.\",\"The submitted diagram clearly shows D unchanged, S1 shifting left/up to S2, and equilibria E1 and E2 consistent with a higher price and lower quantity.\",\"Economic terminology is accurate and applied directly to the wheat-market scenario.\"],\"improvements\":[\"Label the vertical axis “Price of wheat” and the horizontal axis “Quantity of wheat” (and ideally identify the market as wheat) so the equilibrium changes are explicit on the diagram.\"],\"mistakes\":[],\"examinerComment\":\"Estimated practice result: your economic mechanism and written explanation are fully correct. The diagram is also economically correct, but its axes do not identify price and quantity; this limits the overall result under this task’s diagram-label requirement. Your next priority is to label both axes on every market diagram before adding curves and equilibria.\",\"studyNext\":\"Practise fully labelling demand-and-supply diagrams: market/commodity, Price axis, Quantity axis, D, initial and new supply curves, and both equilibria.\",\"assessmentFormat\":\"paper_2_c_to_f_diagram_and_explanation\",\"paper\":\"paper_2\",\"questionPart\":\"unknown\",\"levelRelevance\":\"shared_sl_hl\",\"assessmentSkills\":[\"diagram_explanation\",\"economic_analysis\",\"application\"],\"commandTerm\":\"explain\",\"commandTermLabel\":\"Using a demand and supply diagram, explain\",\"syllabusUnit\":\"unit_2\",\"syllabusTopic\":\"2.3\",\"topicLabel\":\"Competitive market equilibrium\",\"classificationConfidence\":\"high\",\"markingConfidence\":\"high\",\"diagramExpected\":true,\"diagramSubmitted\":true,\"diagramAssessmentStatus\":\"submitted_and_assessed\",\"workingsExpected\":false,\"workingsSubmitted\":false,\"workingsAssessmentStatus\":\"not_relevant\",\"attachmentContent\":\"diagram\",\"assessableEarned\":3,\"markBreakdown\":[{\"label\":\"Diagram\",\"awarded\":3,\"available\":4,\"reason\":\"The diagram correctly shows unchanged D, a leftward shift from S1 to S2, and E2 above and left of E1. However, neither axis is labelled as price or quantity, and wheat is not identified on the diagram.\"},{\"label\":\"Economic analysis\",\"awarded\":4,\"available\":4,\"reason\":\"The written explanation accurately connects the drought to reduced supply at every price, shortage at P1, a rise in price, and lower equilibrium quantity traded.\"},{\"label\":\"Application to context\",\"awarded\":4,\"available\":4,\"reason\":\"The response consistently applies the analysis to wheat harvests and the stated unchanged demand condition.\"}],\"bandRationale\":null,\"limitations\":[],\"componentEvaluation\":{\"diagram\":2,\"explanation\":2,\"diagramReason\":\"A readable, relevant demand-and-supply diagram shows D unchanged and S2 left/up of S1. E2 is higher and left of E1, establishing higher equilibrium price and lower equilibrium quantity. The axes are not named, creating a relevant labeling deficiency.\",\"explanationReason\":\"The explanation fully and coherently links reduced harvests to lower supply, shortage at the original price, a higher equilibrium price, and lower quantity traded.\",\"incompatibleMechanisms\":false,\"mismatchEvidence\":\"\",\"labelingDeficiency\":true,\"labelingEvidence\":\"The vertical and horizontal axes have arrowheads but no labels identifying price of wheat and quantity of wheat; the commodity is also not named on the diagram.\",\"rootErrors\":[]}}"
          }
